    "role": "treasury",
    "question": "What is the Level-2 treasury risk threshold?",
    "response": {
      "answer": "Aggregate counterparty exposure above USD 10,000,000 exceeds the Level-2 treasury risk threshold. [1]\n\nA proposed treasury transaction causing aggregate counterparty exposure above USD 5,000,000 exceeds the Level-1 treasury risk threshold. [2]\n\nFor a Level-2 treasury exposure above USD 10,000,000, notify the Compliance Duty Officer before execution and create an operational risk incident record within one business day. [3]\n\nTreasury Risk Policy version 2.0 is effective on 1 January 2026. [4]\n\nThe new USD 5,000,000 Level-1 threshold applies to current treasury transactions. [5]",
